Break-glass admin account overview:
---
Purpose:
  This admin account is a highly-privileged account that is used in emergencies (hence the "break-glass" name) that is only used when standard admin accounts are experiencing issues.
  This account ensures business continuity while also working to mitigate the elevated risk associated with an account at this level.
---
Account:
  Type:
    -Cloud-only user
    -Role: Global Admin
    -Not synced from on-prem AD
  Name:
    -bg-admin@<redacted_tenant_name>.onmicrosoft.com
    -The naming of this account helps to mitigate accidental use of the account
---
Security Configuration:
  Password:
    -Length: 24+ characters
    -Randomly generated
    -Stored in an offline password vault
    -Roatated every 90 days
    *The length of this password and the password rules help to mitigate cyber risks of this highly privleged account
  *Excluded from MFA to ensure an account can get into the service during MFA service outages
---
Operational Rules:
  -No routine use
  -Not used for testing
  -Only used during designated emergencies
---
Emergency Usage (Examples):
  -MFA service outage
  -Conditional Access policy blocks all admins
  -Corrupted admin accounts
---
Monitoring & Auditing
  Logs
    -All sign ins are monitored via: EntraID sign-in logs and audit logs
  Alerts
    -Alert is triggered with any sign-in attempt
    -These alerts are required to be reviewed by the security team as soon as possible
---
Risk Assessment:
  Identified Risk:
    -Excluding this account from MFA rules increases the chance for a cyberattack if credentials are exposed
  Risk Mitigation:
    -Strong password with regular rotation
    -Offline password storage
    -Continuous monitoring and alerting
    -Regular account log audits
  Risk Acceptance:
    -The fictional organization would accept the risk associated with creating the break-glass account due to the following:
      -Reduced liklihood of tenant lockout
      -Aligned with Microsoft and Zero Trust guidance
